From 7fd178e005c4d3d65975a42120cfb4032f6db909 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ignaciopd3 <210892957+ignaciopd3@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:11:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/26] Casa: the door, the climate and the gas, with messages
 over any channel

A foreground service that reads the devices' status from Tuya's device-sharing
cloud (CloudApi, checked against the official SDK), follows its MQTT reports,
watches the gas sensor on the home network (protocol 3.4, kept open with a
heartbeat), publishes the state for the launcher (CasaProvider) and shows the
door messages (open, still open every 5 minutes, closed) and the gas alarm
(darkened screen, beep, until OK) over whatever is on screen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
